{"candidates":[{"content":"Covering principle: any admissible strengthening of the grounded extension must be a polynomial-time, monotone edge-construction enrichment applied before the skeptical fixed point, never a modification of the fixed-point operator or its derived labels. Weights, bounded defense precomputation, RESIDUE annotations, and re-examination passes all become projections of, or inputs to, this single enrichment layer. Because the enrichment is monotone and polynomial, the fixed point remains deterministic and polynomial; reinstatement remains a theorem about the enriched graph; and committed-root validity is preserved because enrichment is conservative over committed roots—it can add warrants but never deletes or relabels a committed root outside the same fixpoint.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"e093eb8611ff0d96fc197357178adfbf4e9e7c0ba8471f3c76aa9f21a3aea46a"},{"role":"dependence","target":"73c33e65d29d6ed0e48bbb9ae73e4f604fa2682b6f48690875e28e06210dc660"},{"role":"dependence","target":"4fc07d1cf29c58d033683c556e383aabe27935461f789c1c96f95b42883ae66e"},{"role":"dependence","target":"5431feda66e41c92d61607a482c76cb05bd782c10644d596f9f903e82e4e8c2f"},{"role":"dependence","target":"f5a262c5a6bd74029c9528d1063e7a6b5d96c4ee2e4753c79d6fed6817d3fa9b"}],"typicality":0.85},{"content":"Replace Boolean attack with bounded integer weights and define the grounded labeling as the least fixed point of a monotone operator on a finite lattice of (label, weight) pairs, with threshold τ controlling acceptance. Since the lattice is finite and the operator is monotone, the least fixed point is unique and reachable in polynomially many iterations; reinstatement becomes the derived property that a node defended by a chain of sufficiently strong counter-attacks crosses τ. The map from τ to labels is itself monotone, enabling sensitivity analysis without recomputation. Commit only roots whose IN-status is stable under small τ perturbation, preserving committed-root validity.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"4fc07d1cf29c58d033683c556e383aabe27935461f789c1c96f95b42883ae66e"}],"typicality":0.7},{"content":"Add RESIDUE as a fourth derived label that records, for each suspended node, the lexicographically least set of attacking IN-nodes that keep it out; compute it as a pure annotation after the grounded fixed point using a polynomial-time canonical certificate algorithm. This preserves determinism because the fixed point is unchanged and the certificate is canonicalized; it strengthens explainability and gives a constructive witness for every suspension. That witness can later drive a re-examination pass without altering the semantics, and no committed root can be suspended, so committed-root validity is untouched.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"5431feda66e41c92d61607a482c76cb05bd782c10644d596f9f903e82e4e8c2f"}],"typicality":0.6},{"content":"Make reinstatement structural rather than emergent by precomputing defense chains up to a fixed depth d and adding a 'defense edge' from each defender to each node it defends through a chain of length ≤d; then run the ordinary grounded fixpoint on the enriched graph. Because d is fixed, the number of added edges is O(n^{d+1}), so polynomial cost is preserved. Reinstatement is still a derived property—of the enriched graph, not an extra decision rule—and committed-root validity is preserved because the enrichment only makes explicit already-valid defense structure.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"73c33e65d29d6ed0e48bbb9ae73e4f604fa2682b6f48690875e28e06210dc660"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"Allow suspended nodes to be re-examined only through a fresh edge-construction pass that commits new warrants, and make each pass a deterministic polynomial function of the previous graph plus the RESIDUE certificate of the queried node. Bound the number of passes per conjecture by a constant; overall cost remains polynomial, and determinism holds because each pass is a pure function. This unifies SRC_008 with the edge-construction principle: the fixpoint remains the sole decision rule within each pass, and committed roots stay valid because new warrants must themselves be committed before they can relabel a suspended node.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"f5a262c5a6bd74029c9528d1063e7a6b5d96c4ee2e4753c79d6fed6817d3fa9b"}],"typicality":0.4},{"content":"Generalize the grounded extension to a family of fixpoints indexed by a total preorder on warrants, then define the accepted set as the intersection of all fixpoints that respect the preorder—skeptical over orders. The covering principle is that strengthening is choosing a coarser preorder, never changing the underlying attack graph. Because the family is finite and the intersection is computable by a polynomial number of grounded evaluations, determinism and polynomial cost are preserved. Reinstatement and committed-root validity follow from the intersection being a subset of each admissible fixpoint.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"30be11905db881ea7a4e488a8e68f34e4f6b262380bb3b1a31ceb9763a9aea81"},{"role":"dependence","target":"e093eb8611ff0d96fc197357178adfbf4e9e7c0ba8471f3c76aa9f21a3aea46a"},{"role":"dependence","target":"4fc07d1cf29c58d033683c556e383aabe27935461f789c1c96f95b42883ae66e"}],"typicality":0.3}],"simulation_proposals":[]}